        "text": "The diagnosis is internally consistent as far as it goes: a single hypothesis (CPU saturation) with one supporting metric and no contradictions, verdict FAULT, severity high. But it's thin in ways that matter:\n\n- **No recommendations at all.** A high-severity FAULT verdict with zero remediation steps is a gap \u2014 even a generic \"scale out / investigate CPU consumers on checkout\" would follow from the cited evidence.\n- **Single evidence point.** `metric:cpu_high` alone supports \"CPU is high,\" but the causal claim (CPU saturation \u2192 payment timeouts and elevated latency) isn't backed by any latency/timeout metric in the evidence list. The summary asserts more than the cited evidence shows.\n- **Confidence 0.7 vs. severity high.** Reasonable, but the mismatch between moderate confidence and high severity with no unresolved questions is slightly odd \u2014 if confidence is only 0.7, you'd expect at least one open question (e.g., is CPU the cause or a symptom of retry storms?).\n- **No unresolved questions** despite the causal chain being unverified.\n\nNet: coherent but under-supported and incomplete on the action side."
